{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>רב לכם.</b> Like די לכם (enough for you), and the meaning is that you have seized the greater portion." "<b>כי כל העדה כלם קדושים.</b> For all the congregation, from the day of the standing at Mount Sinai, were holy." "<b>ובתוכם ה'.</b> For the Levites were chosen after the Glory was in the midst of the children of Israel. And if Moses knew, when he was at Mount Sinai, that the tribe of Levi was chosen, the children of Israel did not know." "<b>תתנשאו.</b> In that Aaron is the High Priest and Moses is above him, for he taught him."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:55.017362568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}